course: dictionary
lesson: 6913
title: Ozone: one word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the clues in the sentence show which one the writer means. «The ozone layer, high in the sky, blocks much of the Sun's harmful ultraviolet light.» The clues are high in the sky and harmful light, so ozone here is a gas that forms a protective layer.
explain: Ozone can also be a smell. After a thunderstorm, or near the sea, the air can have a sharp, clean smell, and people often call that smell ozone. If a sentence talks about storms or the seaside, check for this meaning.
explain: The word can also mean fresh, clean air. This meaning is informal and a bit old-fashioned, so you might hear a grandad say he needs some ozone after a long day indoors. Ask yourself which meaning fits, then swap it into the sentence to check.
fact: Ozone is a gas made of three oxygen atoms.
fact: High in the sky, the ozone layer protects Earth by blocking much of the Sun's harmful ultraviolet (UV) light.
fact: Some old spray-can and fridge gases damaged the ozone layer and made a hole in it.
fact: In 1987 countries agreed to ban the chemicals that damaged the ozone layer, and it is slowly healing.
fact: Near the ground, ozone is a pollutant that can hurt your lungs, and UV light can still reach you, so wear sunscreen.
exercise: «The ozone layer, high in the sky, blocks much of the Sun's harmful ultraviolet light.» Where is the ozone layer? | Under the sea | Low on the ground, near the trees | *High in the sky | Inside the fridge
exercise: «Those gases were banned by a world agreement in 1987.» What does banned mean? | *Stopped from being used | Made bigger and stronger | Given away for free | Painted bright red
exercise: After the thunderstorm the air had a sharp, clean smell. What is that smell often called? | Sweet smoke | Mud | Lava | *Ozone
test: «Yet when the world agreed to act, the ozone layer began to heal.» What does heal mean here? | Get hotter | Break into pieces | Turn green | *Get better and mend
test: «Near the ground ozone is a pollutant that can hurt your lungs.» What is a pollutant? | A famous scientist | A kind of sunscreen | *Something that dirties the air and can harm us | A type of cloud
exam: «The ozone layer protects Earth from harmful sunlight.» Which meaning of ozone fits this sentence? | *A gas high in the sky | Fresh clean air on a walk | A smell like a birthday cake | A kind of rain
